Z||000000||jlhuber||01-24-2000||10:27 PM||||my baby is dyin'.  i'm getting 10 mpg, extremely low oil pressure, and a horrible sound internally from the 2.8.  it is hard to decribe the sound, kinda a combo of grind/rattle/knock. it used to have an annoying rattle a little while ago that i am told was just a loose rocker arm.  two oil changes ago i used valvoline sae 30 racing oil, why? i dunno.  ever since i have noticed quite low oil pressure.  but just recently i have noticed the excessive fuel consumption and worsening sound.  i am now scared to drive it in fear that it may leave me stranded or at worst, blow up.  anyway, a mechanic buddy of mine says it sounds like a loose rocker arm and possibly a busted exhaust valve.  my question is could a busted valve cause all or some of my problems.  the motor is the 2.8 with 79k original miles with one rebuild on 4-14-97 from an "engine knock"||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-24-2000||11:02 PM||||If the rocker arm fell off then the lifter got launched out of its bore and the oil no longer pressurizes anything past that bore on that side of the engine--that includes bearings.  That grinding sound is caused by grinding, pieces of hot metal tearing off other pieces of hot metal without benefit of lubrication.  The Fiero will definitely go boom and quit soon.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||01-24-2000||11:09 PM||||Jeez, already rebuit once?  Only 79k? I think that I would sh*tcan that motor and rebuild a junkyar donor, that engine has some bad mojo workin on it!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||jlhuber||01-24-2000||11:56 PM||||i am now thinking that when it was rebuilt the first time, someone did not do something quite right.  it was not me either, it was taken to a shop by the previous owner.  i am working on putting a 3800 series II s/c into it, but have not yet found a suitable donor car, and my finances are kinda limited at the current moment.  they are even more limited now that i can't get to my second job.  though i am also currently trying to get a better paying closer 2nd job so i can take better care of my baby.  anywho, i am going to find out this weekend how bad the damage is.  thanks for the replies.  later||||reg||1
